dynotiq (0.2~beta1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Dyno records what the machine waits for: CPU, memory and disk stalls from
    the kernel pressure counters, the run queue wait of the game process and
    its paging accesses. New PAGING verdict for stutter without any heat.
  * Throttling reason now comes from the driver instead of the temperature,
    and AMD cards get a verdict at all for the first time.
  * Game check knows ntsync and Resizable BAR.
  * Steam: titles pointing at a Proton build that is not installed, and
    prefixes left behind by uninstalled games.
  * New incidents: ext4 errors, NVMe resets, uncorrectable PCIe errors, page
    flip failures, AMD ring timeouts and applications killed by systemd-oomd.
  * App check explains journal lines, and its search matches inside a name.
  * Fixes: the dyno filed runs under the runtime or the Proton build instead
    of the game, measuring threads could overlap, throttling was timed from
    the start of the recording, and AMD had no VRAM, power or throttle values.

 -- simonlinuxcraft <simonlinuxcraft@pm.me>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 21:15:00 +0200

